        <body>
            <div xml:id="d181">

                <pb facs="0381" n="333" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg333"/>

                <head>No. 181.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Count Litta to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Italy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1877-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 26, 1877</date>.
                        (Received May 26.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: Referring to the
                    conversation which I had the honor to have with you day before yesterday, I
                    hasten herewith to transmit to you a copy of the proclamation of neutrality
                    which appeared in the Official Gazette of the kingdom of the 28th ultimo.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, Mr. Secretary of State, the assurances of the very high
                    consideration with which I have the honor to be,</p>
                <p>Very truly, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed>LITTA.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d181-a1.xml" xpointer="d181-a1"/>
            </div>
